    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can a snake plant live in a room with no window?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A snake plant can live in a room with no window only under good electric light, because it needs some light to make its food. Under bright LED or office lighting that is on for long hours, a snake plant survives but grows very slowly. In a room that stays dark it uses up its stored reserves and dies, so move it to a window if it stops growing, fades or leans."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does a snake plant clean the air?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A snake plant does not noticeably clean the air in a normal room. Studies that found snake plants removing chemicals were done in small sealed chambers, and a home would need far more plants than anyone keeps to match fresh air from ventilation. Buy it because it looks good and is easy to keep, not as an air filter."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can a snake plant live outside in the UAE?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, a snake plant can live outside in the UAE in shade, and it grows well outdoors from October to April. From May to September keep it in full shade, out of the midday and afternoon sun, and test the soil more often in heatwaves, because pots dry out fast. Move it outside gradually, not straight from an AC room. In winter it is happy on the coast, but inland and in colder GCC cities protect it from nights below about 10–13 °C."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Is a snake plant good for the bedroom?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, a snake plant is a practical bedroom plant. It copes with low light and AC rooms, needs little care, and unlike most plants it takes in carbon dioxide at night. One snake plant will not noticeably change the air in a room."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can a snake plant grow in water?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A snake plant can be kept in water with only the roots submerged, and leaf cuttings root in water. Change the water often to keep it clean (UConn Extension advises daily for rooting cuttings) and keep the leaves dry. In water it grows more slowly and less reliably than in free-draining soil, so pot it up if it starts to struggle."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does a snake plant flower?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A snake plant flowers only occasionally, and snake plants kept indoors rarely flower. Older plants sometimes send up a stalk of small, fragrant, greenish-white to cream flowers."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How long does a snake plant live?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "With basic care a snake plant lives for many years, and it keeps producing new shoots that you can divide into new plants."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why is a snake plant a popular gift in the UAE?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A snake plant forgives missed waterings and looks good in modern homes and offices. That makes it a common housewarming, Eid and corporate gift."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How is plant size measured?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Size is measured from the bottom of the nursery pot to the top tip of the highest leaf. A plant listed as 50-60 CM stands in that range measured this way."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Which pot option should I choose, nursery or decorative?",
